  "severity": "critical",
  "kind": "ca_compromise",
  "summary": "Eight eMudhra (emSign) intermediate CAs, sixteen certificates including Sectigo AAA cross-signs, were issued with keys that can be recovered from the certificates themselves. Anyone can mint TLS or code-signing certificates for any name that chains to those intermediates. The intermediates are revoked, but most clients do not check revocation, so any trust store that still contains an anchoring root accepts forged certificates.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "wahp",
      "title": "eMudhra: we have a problem (Dennis Jackson)",
      "url": "https://emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com/",
